# --- Original Caesar (1992) game assets — NEVER commit these. ---
# See CLAUDE.md "Critical rule before touching anything" / GAIUS_MASTERPLAN.md
# section 3 (IP posture). Tests/tools read these from a directory pointed at
# by the GAIUS_TEST_ASSETS env var, which lives outside this repo entirely —
# these patterns are a safety net, not the primary defense.
*.VPX
*.vpx
*.PL8
*.pl8
*.PL1
*.pl1
*.P32
*.p32
*.256
# The scenario data files are EMPIRE2.000-EMPIRE2.049, so match the numeric
# extension specifically rather than "EMPIRE2.*". The broad glob silently
# swallowed our OWN decoder sources (formats/empire2/empire2.cpp/.hpp) for
# two commits, because core.ignorecase is true on Windows/macOS and so
# "EMPIRE2.*" matched "empire2.cpp" -- which meant a fresh clone was
# missing a file CMakeLists.txt requires and could not build at all.
EMPIRE2.[0-9][0-9][0-9]
empire2.[0-9][0-9][0-9]
# Belt-and-braces: never ignore our own source, whatever the patterns above
# grow into later.
!formats/empire2/*.cpp
!formats/empire2/*.hpp
*.SAV
*.sav
CSR.EXE
csr.exe
COHORT.EXE
COHORT.CSR
EDATA.CSR
CONTFRM.GD8
